{"name":"Yew Hedge","hex":"#656952","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"yew","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of coniferous tree, Taxus baccata, with dark-green flat needle-like leaves and seeds bearing red arils, native to western, central and southern Europe, northwest Africa, northern Iran and southwest Asia.","Any tree or shrub of the genus Taxus."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made from the wood of the yew tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yew"},{"term":"hedge","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thicket of bushes or other shrubbery, especially one planted as a fence between two portions of land, or to separate the parts of a garden.","A barrier (often consisting of a line of persons or objects) to protect someone or something from harm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose with a hedge or hedges.","To obstruct or surround."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hedge"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yew","blocks":[{"text":"Yew is a common name given to various species of trees."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Taxaceae_taxonomic_diagram_2.png/330px-Taxaceae_taxonomic_diagram_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yew"},{"title":"Hedge","blocks":[{"text":"A hedge or hedgerow is a line of shrubs and sometimes trees, planted and trained to form a barrier or to mark the boundary of an area, such as between neighbouring properties. Hedges that are used to separate a road from adjoining fields or one field from another, and are of sufficient age to incorporate larger trees, are known as hedgerows. Often they serve as windbreaks to improve conditions for the adjacent crops, as in bocage country. When clipped and maintained, hedges are also a simple form of topiary. Hedges and Hedgerows are usually no wider than about three feet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Rotbuchenhecke_in_der_Eifel.jpg/330px-Rotbuchenhecke_in_der_Eifel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hedge"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Taxus_globosa_foliage.jpg/330px-Taxus_globosa_foliage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Taxus_globosa_foliage.jpg/330px-Taxus_globosa_foliage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Foliage of a Mexican yew","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATaxus_globosa_foliage.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Senecio_angulatus_shrub_form.jpg/500px-Senecio_angulatus_shrub_form.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Senecio_angulatus_shrub_form.jpg/500px-Senecio_angulatus_shrub_form.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A round hedge of creeping groundsel","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASenecio_angulatus_shrub_form.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Littlestane_march_dyke.JPG/500px-Littlestane_march_dyke.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Littlestane_march_dyke.JPG/1280px-Littlestane_march_dyke.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Littlestane_march_dyke.JPG/500px-Littlestane_march_dyke.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A typical old Scottish march dyke, but without boundary trees","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALittlestane_march_dyke.